-- Declarative animation: sprites that declare their own `frames` (+ optional `fps`)
-- cycle by themselves, so the drawn pixels change frame by frame.
hero is {x: 20, y: 20, frames: ["hero", "coin"], fps: 60}
thing is {x: 60, y: 60, frames: ["coin", "heart", "hero"], fps: 15}
to update
  tick is 1
to draw
  clear screen to black
  draw sprite hero at hero.x, hero.y
  draw sprite thing at thing.x, thing.y
run game with update and draw
